    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d418">

                <pb facs="0468" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/3057: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Bolivia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Woodward</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">La Paz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-03T16:00:00-04:00">May 3, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:24 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>994. Cuenca<anchor n="74" xml:id="d418-f1"/> mentioned to Ashton<anchor n="75"
                        xml:id="d418-f2"/> of the British Legation that Baldivieso had stated that
                    the Provisional Government would probably <pb facs="0469" n="455" xml:id="pg455"
                    /> promptly release the persons accused of plotting a revolution and raise the
                    state of siege if the Provisional Government were to be recognized.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Woodward</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d418-f1" n="74" xml:id="d418-f1-content">
                <p>Humberto Cuenca, Manager of the Central Bank of Bolivia.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d418-f2" n="75" xml:id="d418-f2-content">
                <p>Anthony Ashton, of the British Legation in Bolivia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
